---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Privacy Policy — DevFest.cz 2026"
	description="Privacy policy for DevFest.cz 2026 — how we collect, use, and protect your personal data."
	showFooter={false}
>
	<main class="policy">
		<div class="policy-inner">
			<a href="/" class="back-link">&#8592; Back</a>

			<h1 class="policy-title">Privacy Policy</h1>
			<p class="policy-meta eyebrow">GUG.cz, z.s. · Last updated: October 2026</p>

			<section>
				<h2>1. Who we are</h2>
				<p>
					DevFest.cz 2026 is organised by GUG.cz, z.s. (formerly GDG Czech Republic),
					a registered association (zapsaný spolek) and the data controller for the
					personal data described here. For privacy-related enquiries, contact us at <a href="mailto:devfest@gug.cz">devfest@gug.cz</a>.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2>2. Data we collect and why</h2>

				<h3>a) Newsletter sign-up</h3>
				<p>
					When you submit your email address via the notification form, we store it in
					SmartEmailing (our email service provider) to send you conference updates such as
					ticket availability announcements and event news. Legal basis: consent (GDPR Art. 6(1)(a)).
					You may unsubscribe at any time via the link in every email.
				</p>

				<h3>b) Analytics</h3>
				<p>
					We use Google Firebase Analytics (measurement ID G-L5NK2S2EZ0) to understand how
					visitors use the site, so we can improve it. It runs only if you accept analytics
					cookies in the cookie banner.
				</p>
				<p>
					<strong>Before you decide, and if you decline:</strong> analytics does not run. The
					site loads no Google Analytics code, sets no analytics cookie, and sends Google no
					measurement data about your visit.
				</p>
				<p>
					<strong>If you accept:</strong> analytics loads and sets the <code>_ga</code> cookies listed below, which give you a random analytics identifier.
					That lets us count returning visitors and follow sessions across pages — pages
					visited, session duration, browser type. We never collect your name, email, or any
					other information that identifies you personally. Legal basis: consent
					(GDPR Art. 6(1)(a)). You can withdraw consent at any time by clicking "Decline" in
					the cookie banner (clear your browser storage to see it again).
				</p>
				<p>
					Alongside page views we also record a few interaction events:
					opening the ticket checkout, completing a newsletter sign-up or a ticket purchase,
					and submitting a company invoice request. These record the action itself — which
					ticket wave, its price, how many tickets — and never your name, email, company
					details, or anything else that identifies you.
				</p>
				<p>
					The data is used only for analytics — never for advertising,
					ad personalisation, or profiling.
				</p>

				<h3>c) Server logs</h3>
				<p>
					Our hosting provider (Firebase Hosting) automatically records standard access logs
					(IP address, browser, requested URL). These are retained for up to 30 days for
					security purposes. Legal basis: legitimate interests (GDPR Art. 6(1)(f)).
				</p>

				<h3>d) Bot protection (reCAPTCHA)</h3>
				<p>
					To protect our ticketing data from automated scraping and abuse, the site uses
					Google reCAPTCHA Enterprise (via Firebase App Check). reCAPTCHA runs in the background to
					tell humans from bots, analysing signals such as your interactions with the page,
					device and browser information, and IP address. This data is shared with Google and
					processed under the <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Privacy Policy</a> and <a href="https://policies.google.com/terms" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Terms of Service</a>.
					Because this is a security measure, it runs regardless of your cookie choice.
					Legal basis: legitimate interests (GDPR Art. 6(1)(f)).
				</p>

				<h3>e) Company invoice requests</h3>
				<p>
					If you request a company invoice via the <a href="/invoice">company invoice form</a>, we collect your company name,
					registration number (IČO), VAT identification number (DIČ, if provided),
					billing address (street, city, ZIP, country), contact email, and the number of
					tickets requested. We use this data to issue the invoice, process your payment,
					and send you a discount code to claim your tickets on ti.to. The request is
					stored in Google Firestore, the invoice is issued through iDoklad, and the
					discount code is created in ti.to. Legal basis: performance of a contract
					(GDPR Art. 6(1)(b)) and compliance with our legal accounting and tax
					obligations (GDPR Art. 6(1)(c)). Issued invoices and related accounting
					records are retained for up to 10 years, as required by Czech tax and
					accounting law.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2>3. Cookies</h2>
				<p>We use the following cookies:</p>
				<!-- A data table is one of the things WCAG 1.4.10 exempts from
				     single-column reflow: it needs two dimensions to be read at
				     all. So the TABLE scrolls sideways, not the page. Focusable
				     because a scrollable region must be reachable by keyboard
				     (WCAG 2.1.1); labelled because it is now a landmark. -->
				<div class="table-scroll" role="region" aria-label="Cookies we set" tabindex="0">
				<table>
					<caption class="sr-only">List of cookies we set, their purpose, and retention period.</caption>
					<thead>
						<tr>
							<th scope="col">Name</th>
							<th scope="col">Purpose</th>
							<th scope="col">Duration</th>
						</tr>
					</thead>
					<tbody>
						<tr>
							<th scope="row"><code>cookie-consent</code></th>
							<td>Stores your cookie preference (localStorage)</td>
							<td>Until you clear browser storage</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<th scope="row"><code>_ga, _ga_*</code></th>
							<td>Google Analytics — only set after consent</td>
							<td>2 years</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<th scope="row"><code>_GRECAPTCHA</code></th>
							<td>Google reCAPTCHA — bot protection (set for security, not consent-gated)</td>
							<td>6 months</td>
						</tr>
					</tbody>
				</table>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2>4. Data sharing</h2>
				<p>
					We do not sell your data. We share it only with the processors listed below, under
					data processing agreements and only to the extent necessary to provide the
					services described:
				</p>
				<ul>
					<li>SmartEmailing — newsletter delivery</li>
					<li>Google Firebase (Hosting, Analytics, Firestore) — website hosting, analytics, and storage of invoice requests</li>
					<li>Google reCAPTCHA Enterprise (via Firebase App Check) — bot protection</li>
					<li>iDoklad (Solitea a.s. / Seyfor, <a href="https://www.idoklad.cz" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">idoklad.cz</a>) — issuing company invoices</li>
					<li>ti.to — ticket sales and discount-code redemption</li>
				</ul>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2>5. Your rights</h2>
				<p>Under GDPR you have the right to:</p>
				<ul>
					<li>Access the personal data we hold about you</li>
					<li>Request correction or deletion of your data</li>
					<li>Withdraw consent at any time (this does not affect prior processing)</li>
					<li>Lodge a complaint with the Czech Data Protection Authority (<a href="https://www.uoou.cz" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">uoou.cz</a>)</li>
				</ul>
				<p>To exercise these rights, email us at <a href="mailto:devfest@gug.cz">devfest@gug.cz</a>.</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2>6. Changes to this policy</h2>
				<p>
					We may update this policy as the website evolves. The "last updated" date at the top
					reflects the most recent revision. Material changes will be announced via our newsletter.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section id="mobile-app">
				<h2>7. Mobile app</h2>
				<p>
					This section covers the DevFest.cz mobile app for iOS and Android (bundle and
					package id <code>cz.devfest.app</code>). The data controller is the same as for the
					website: GUG.cz, z.s., <a href="mailto:devfest@gug.cz">devfest@gug.cz</a>. The app
					is not directed at children.
				</p>
				<p>
					You can use the programme without logging in. Logging in with your ticket is
					optional and is needed only for networking and for keeping your favourites on
					your account.
				</p>

				<h3>a) What the app collects and why</h3>
				<!-- Same sideways-scrolling table as the cookie list in section 3. -->
				<div class="table-scroll" role="region" aria-label="Data the mobile app collects" tabindex="0">
				<table>
					<caption class="sr-only">Data the mobile app collects, where it comes from, why, and how long it is kept.</caption>
					<thead>
						<tr>
							<th scope="col">Data</th>
							<th scope="col">Source</th>
							<th scope="col">Purpose</th>
							<th scope="col">Retention</th>
						</tr>
					</thead>
					<tbody>
						<tr>
							<th scope="row">Registration reference / ti.to ticket code</th>
							<td>Typed by you, or read from your ticket's QR code, when you log in with your ticket</td>
							<td>Look up your ticket in the ti.to check-in list</td>
							<td>Until the account is deleted</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<th scope="row">Full name and email address</th>
							<td>Taken from the matched ti.to ticket, never typed in the app</td>
							<td>Your account and ticket verification</td>
							<td>Until the account is deleted</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<th scope="row">6-digit email verification code</th>
							<td>Generated by our backend and sent to the ticket email via Resend</td>
							<td>Confirm that you own the ticket email</td>
							<td>Stored only as a salted hash, expires after 30 minutes, purged nightly</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<th scope="row">Favourite session ids</th>
							<td>Your taps in the agenda (ids of public programme sessions)</td>
							<td>Your personal agenda and session reminders</td>
							<td>Until the account is deleted</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<th scope="row">Networking connections: the name and company of each attendee whose badge you scan (what the badge already prints), their ticket identifier and the time of the scan. Never their email</th>
							<td>The QR code on the other attendee's badge, scanned by you after logging in with your ticket</td>
							<td>Your list of people you met. After the conference we email you that list via Resend</td>
							<td>At most 500 entries, until your account is deleted</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<th scope="row">Account metadata (Firebase user id, created and updated timestamps)</th>
							<td>Firebase Authentication</td>
							<td>Run your account</td>
							<td>Until the account is deleted</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<th scope="row">Usage analytics: screen views and a closed set of events (tab switched, session opened, session favourited or unfavourited, onboarding finished), app-instance id, device model, OS version, coarse location derived from IP address</th>
							<td>Firebase Analytics</td>
							<td>Understand how the app is used. No user id is set, no event contains personal data, and the advertising ID is not collected</td>
							<td>14 months (Google default)</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<th scope="row">Crash reports: stack traces, device model, OS version, installation id</th>
							<td>Firebase Crashlytics</td>
							<td>Fix crashes</td>
							<td>90 days (Google default)</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<th scope="row">Device attestation signals</th>
							<td>Firebase App Check with Play Integrity (Android) or App Attest (Apple)</td>
							<td>Protect our backend from abuse</td>
							<td>As set by Google and Apple for each platform</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<th scope="row">Push notification subscriptions: topics for announcements, general sessions and one per favourited session</th>
							<td>Firebase Cloud Messaging. The device token is held by Google and is never stored in our database</td>
							<td>Send announcements and reminders for sessions you favourited. Notification permission is optional</td>
							<td>Until you unsubscribe, turn notifications off or uninstall the app</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<th scope="row">App update check: app id, app version, platform and a random per-install id</th>
							<td>Sent to Shorebird when the app starts</td>
							<td>Deliver code updates to the app</td>
							<td>As set by Shorebird</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<th scope="row">Backend logs, which can contain your user id and the matched ticket email</th>
							<td>Google Cloud Logging</td>
							<td>Operate and debug the backend</td>
							<td>30 days</td>
						</tr>
					</tbody>
				</table>
				</div>

				<h3>b) Networking: if your badge is scanned</h3>
				<p>
					Another attendee who is logged in to the app can scan the QR code on your badge.
					If they do, the person who scanned it gets your name and company, the same details
					your badge already shows, and the app keeps them on that person's account. Your
					email address is never shared. After the conference we email each attendee the list
					of people they scanned. The entry is deleted when the person who scanned you deletes
					their account, and you can ask us to remove it earlier (see section 8).
				</p>

				<h3>c) Camera</h3>
				<p>
					The app uses the camera only to scan a ticket or badge QR code. The camera frames
					are processed on your device and are not uploaded or stored. On Android, scanning
					uses Google's ML Kit barcode model, and Google receives its own usage telemetry
					from ML Kit.
				</p>

				<h3>d) Stored only on your device</h3>
				<p>
					Whether you finished onboarding, which reminder topics you chose, and an inbox of up
					to 100 received notifications are kept in the app's storage on your device. They
					never reach our servers, are not backed up, and are removed when you uninstall the
					app.
				</p>

				<h3>e) Legal basis</h3>
				<p>
					The account, ticket verification, personal agenda, networking connections and push
					notifications are processed to provide the app you asked for (GDPR Art. 6(1)(b)).
					Usage analytics, crash reports, device attestation, update checks and backend logs
					are processed on the basis of our legitimate interests
					in keeping the app working, secure and useful (GDPR Art. 6(1)(f)).
				</p>

				<h3>f) Analytics and crash reports are always on</h3>
				<p>
					Unlike the website, the app has no consent switch: usage analytics and crash
					reporting are always on, and there is no in-app opt-out. They carry no name, email
					or user id, and they are never used for advertising, ad personalisation or tracking.
					If you do not want them sent, please do not use the app.
				</p>

				<h3>g) Processors</h3>
				<p>
					We do not sell app data, do not share it with third parties acting as independent
					controllers, and do not use it for advertising or tracking. All data is encrypted in
					transit. It is processed only by:
				</p>
				<ul>
					<li>Google (Firebase Authentication, Firestore, Realtime Database, Cloud Functions, Analytics, Crashlytics, Cloud Messaging, App Check / Play Integrity, ML Kit, Cloud Logging) — running the app and its backend</li>
					<li>Apple (App Attest, push notification delivery, App Store) — device attestation, notifications and app distribution on iOS</li>
					<li>ti.to — ticket lookup</li>
					<li>Resend — sending the verification email and the post-conference list of people you scanned</li>
					<li>Shorebird — app code updates</li>
				</ul>
				<p>
					Your rights from section 5 apply to app data too.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section id="delete-account">
				<h2>8. Deleting your app account</h2>
				<p>
					<strong>In the app:</strong> go to Profile &gt; Delete account. This immediately
					deletes your Firebase Authentication account, your user record (name, email,
					registration reference, favourite sessions and networking connections) and any
					pending verification codes.
				</p>
				<p>
					<strong>Without the app:</strong> email <a href="mailto:devfest@gug.cz?subject=Delete%20my%20DevFest%20app%20account">devfest@gug.cz</a> from
					the email address on your ticket with the subject "Delete my DevFest app account".
					We delete the same data within 30 days.
				</p>
				<p>
					<strong>What is not deleted:</strong> usage analytics, crash reports and App Check
					signals are not linked to your account, so they cannot be picked out and deleted;
					they expire on their own (analytics after 14 months, crash reports after 90 days).
					Data kept only on your device goes away when you uninstall the app. If another
					attendee scanned your badge, your name and company stay in their list until they
					delete their account; email <a href="mailto:devfest@gug.cz">devfest@gug.cz</a> and we
					will remove them. Your ti.to ticket itself is not affected.
				</p>
				<p>
					The same instructions are on a page of their own at <a href="/delete-account">devfest.cz/delete-account</a>.
				</p>
			</section>
		</div>
	</main>
</BaseLayout>

<style lang="scss">
	@use './privacy-policy';
</style>
